From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Peble <phil@peble.net>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 23:14:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(build): drop the readme field and unpin hatchling

Replaces the temporary `hatchling<1.32` pin from 767681ba3 with the actual
fix. hatchling 1.32.0 rejects a `readme` resolving outside the project
directory, and both packages pointed at ../README.md.

Delete the field rather than relocate the file. It only populates the
Description in package metadata, which matters when a package is
published, and neither of these is: there is no publish step in build-aux
or the workflows, and both are uv workspace members resolved from a local
path and installed editable. python/README.md is also the 265-line
"Ambassador Developer's Guide", which is not this package's description in
any case.

Verified against hatchling==1.32.0 exactly: the previous config fails with
"Readme path must be within the project directory: ../README.md", and both
packages build with the field removed. `uv sync --dev`, the command CI's
Install Deps step runs, also succeeds -- that exercises build_editable,
which is the hook that was failing rather than build_wheel.

Backport to v4.1.0: v4.1.0 never carried the hatchling<1.32 pin, so only
the readme removal applies.

(cherry picked from commit 0763f1e3803f332af78bb5059f6372a4c05a591d)
Signed-off-by: Phil Peble <phil@peble.net>
---
 python/ambassador-diag/pyproject.toml | 1 -
 python/ambassador/pyproject.toml      | 1 -
 2 files changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/ambassador-diag/pyproject.toml b/python/ambassador-diag/pyproject.toml
index 8ebbe9d35..521d9acc2 100644
--- a/python/ambassador-diag/pyproject.toml
+++ b/python/ambassador-diag/pyproject.toml
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 [project]
 name = "ambassador_diag"
 version = "4.0.0-dev"
-readme = "../README.md"
 dependencies = [
     "click",
     "flask",
diff --git a/python/ambassador/pyproject.toml b/python/ambassador/pyproject.toml
index e51869d57..1d79dc7bd 100644
--- a/python/ambassador/pyproject.toml
+++ b/python/ambassador/pyproject.toml
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 [project]
 name = "ambassador"
 version = "4.0.0-dev"
-readme = "../README.md"
 dependencies = [
     "orjson",
     "pyyaml",
